  "scope": "Prepared complete C0 point and uniform C1 box source/provenance/event boundary at8..20 only. Every actual run remains provisional until complete native and canonical source/input/binary/tube/guard/event/full-variation and arithmetic evidence is independently checked. This component admission does not accept any completed32/64 return.",
  "sourceArgument": [
    "The full-return C++ differs from the reviewed sparse supplier only by the exact-zero selector/types. The recurrence omits complete outward zero Taylor Jacobian coefficients only, preserving every nonzero coefficient and every global variation column. Pinned CAPD C0/C1 doubleton movement, approved remainders, curve and first ascending coordinate-event machinery remain unchanged.",
    "The new V4 target checker pins the separately approved order20 source audit and all its exact dependencies, prepared full-return C++/runner, original/base/selector headers, all440 CAPD headers, library, model/source/scales/physical decimal centers, exact coupling and fixed q_N. It admits only matched C0 point or uniform C1 box commands, exact compile flags, radius/mode/order and runtime resource contracts.",
    "The wrapper and strict adapter require the three actual supplier headers for both stages, compare every initial/image/endpoint field/time/raw variation and full tube/guard range with the separately hashed native originals, verify exact center/box coverage and every complete137N domain obligation, enforce strict positive crossing slopes and rooted whole branch time coverage, and recompute all section derivatives from the full18N raw fixed-time variation.",
    "The uniform existence derivative remains mandatory and unchanged. Unadmitted large exact-K, affine and order28 suppliers explicitly reject. Future point28 pairing requires a separately reviewed new wrapper version.",
    "Mock command/source fixtures only establish parser and binding controls. No mock flow or source-shaped artifact establishes a completed return. The already admitted method argument supplies recurrence soundness; no interval overlap or timing speed comparison is used as correctness proof."
  ],
